"""
sales_banner.py
===============

Award / recognition banner generator for the Sales platform.

WHY THIS IS BUILT THE WAY IT IS
-------------------------------
Generative image models *always* redraw faces. There is no prompt that reliably
stops it. So we never send the employee photos to the image model at all.

Pipeline ("plate + composite"):

    1. Text LLM  -> writes an image prompt for a BACKGROUND PLATE ONLY.
                    No people, no faces, no text, no logos. Just an empty,
                    designed stage with reserved clean zones.
    2. Gemini    -> renders that plate at the requested aspect ratio.
                    (If it fails, we fall back to a procedural gradient plate,
                    so the endpoint never hard-fails.)
    3. Pillow    -> deterministically composites, in this order:
                       title -> description -> recipient cards
                       (photo + name + achievement) -> logo
                    Photos are pasted pixel-exact, then *harmonised* (tint,
                    luminance and grain matched to the local background) so
                    they sit in the design instead of looking stuck on.
    4. Logo      -> the flat-black Zensar mark is recoloured to white or black
                    by measuring the luminance actually under it.

Everything the user must be able to read (title, names, achievements) is
rendered as real vector text, so it is never garbled and never misspelled.

INTEGRATION NOTES
-----------------
* The React modal (SalesBannerGenerator.tsx) expects JSON, not a PNG stream:
      { "success": true, "image_base64": "<...>" }
  handle_sales_banner() returns exactly that. The sample banner.py returns a
  raw Response(media_type="image/png") -- that shape will NOT work with the
  existing frontend.
* Relative imports below mirror sample banner.py. Adjust the dots if this file
  lives at a different depth.
* Drop brand fonts (Montserrat / Poppins / Inter TTFs) into FONT_DIR and they
  are picked up automatically. Otherwise DejaVu is used.
"""

